WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.802
F

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:05.438 line:78%
THE ATTACKS.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:07.640 line:78%
PRESIDENT BIDEN SAYS THAT TEXAS

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.241 line:78%
ABORTION LAW IS AN UNAMERICAN

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.209 line:78%
VIGILANTE SYSTEM.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.910 line:78%
THE SUPREME COURT HAS REFUSED TO

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.213 line:78%
STOP THE NEW REGULATIONS.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.280 line:78%
AND THAT'S INTENSIFYING

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.282 line:78%
DEMOCRATIC EFFORTS TO CHANGE THE

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:17.784 line:78%
MAKEUP OF THE HIGH COURT AND GET

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.618 line:78%
RID OF THE SENATE FILIBUSTER.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.253 line:78%
WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT PETER

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:22.055 line:78%
DOOCY HAS THE LATEST ON THAT

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:26.593 line:78%
TONIGHT.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:28.228 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I HAVE BEEN CONTINUE TO BE A

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.896 line:78%
STRONG SUPPORTER OF ROE V. WADE.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.698 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND BEFORE ROE V. WADE IS

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.432 line:78%
CHALLENGED IN FRONT OF THE

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.134 line:78%
SUPREME COURT, PRESIDENT BIDEN

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:36.569 line:78%
IS WORRIED BECAUSE THEY, JUST

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.936 line:78%
UPHELD A TEXAS LAW RESTRICTING

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.471 line:78%
ABORTION.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.141 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE MOST PERNICIOUS THING

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:44.244 line:78%
ABOUT THE TEXAS LAW IS SORT OF

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:48.782 line:78%
CREATES A VIGILANTE SYSTEM WHERE

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:49.115 line:78%
PEOPLE GET REWARDS TO GO OUT --

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.918 line:78%
ANYWAY.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:53.319 line:78%
AND IT JUST SEEMS -- I KNOW THIS

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.720 line:78%
SOUNDS RIDICULOUS, ALMOST

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.188 line:78%
UNAMERICAN.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.323 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PROGRESSIVES HAVE HAD IT.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:58.858 line:78%
AOC TWEETS:  REPUBLICANS PROMISE

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.626 line:78%
TO OVERTURN ROE V. WADE AND THEY

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.727 line:78%
HAVE.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:02.462 line:78%
DEMOCRATS CAN EITHER ABOLISH THE

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:03.696 line:78%
FILIBUSTER AND EXPAND THE COURT

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.498 line:78%
OR DO NOTHING.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.566 line:78%
SOME PROGRESSIVES HAVE ALREADY

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:09.035 line:78%
OUTLINED HOW THEY WOULD DO IT.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:11.871 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE UNDO THE DAMAGE,

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.073 line:78%
REPUBLICANS HAVE DONE BY

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:16.609 line:78%
RESTORING BALANCE AND WE DO IT

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:17.677 line:78%
BY PASSING THE JUDICIARY ACT OF

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.313 line:78%
2021 TO ADD FOUR SEATS TO THE

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:21.347 line:78%
COURT TO CREATE A 13-MEMBER

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.615 line:78%
SUPREME COURT.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.916 line:78%
&gt;&gt; PRESIDENT DESCRIBES HIMSELF

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.750 line:78%
AS A.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:26.019 line:78%
&gt;&gt; STUDENT OF HISTORY.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.521 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND HISTORICALLY BEEN AGAINST

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.922 line:78%
EXPANDING THE COURT LIKE WHEN

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.824 line:78%
FDR TRIED.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:33.326 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE VIOLATED NO LAW.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.760 line:78%
HE WAS LEGALISTICALLY ABSOLUTELY

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.962 line:78%
CORRECT.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.964 line:78%
BUT IT WAS A BONE HEADED IDEA.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:39.265 line:78%
&gt;&gt; BUT AS PRESIDENT, HE HAS

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:41.401 line:78%
ORDERED A COMMISSION OF EXPERTS

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:43.036 line:78%
TO BRIEF HIM ON THE PROS AND

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.104 line:78%
CONS OF COURT PACKING.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.805 line:78%
AND IN HIS MIND IS OPEN.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.006 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE PRESIDENT DOESN'T HAVE

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.540 line:78%
ANY THOUGHTS ON THE STRUCTURE OF

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.675 line:78%
THE COURT.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.509 line:78%
&gt;&gt; HE'S WAITING FOR THE

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.644 line:78%
CONCLUSION OF THIS REPORT.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:53.847 line:78%
LOOKS FORWARD TO REVIEWING IT.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.547 line:78%
SEEING WHERE THEY COME OUT.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.015 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Pete: IF THE PRESIDENT

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.717 line:78%
DECIDES HE WANTS TO ADD FOUR

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.119 line:78%
SPOTS TO THE COURT AND FILL THEM

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:02.288 line:78%
WITH PROGRESSIVES, HE IS GOING

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:04.224 line:78%
TO HAVE TO DO IT WHILE DEMOCRATS

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.925 line:78%
CONTROL CONGRESS WHICH COULD

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:08.161 line:78%
MAKE THE FIGHT AHEAD THE

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:09.095 line:78%
UPCOMING MIDTERMS THE EQUIVALENT

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.095 line:78%
OF A KWAME KAVANAUGH

